-# Texture Studio
+# mPainter
 
-A native texturing application in development: a Substance Painter-style Qt interface and Blender-fork EEVEE/GPU, mesh/UV and `.blend` code linked in the same process. Our paint engine owns layers, masks, channels and stroke transactions. A compatible ordinary-Blender add-on remains part of the goal.
+mPainter is a GPL-licensed 3D texture painting application by Mattias Lind. It combines a Qt workspace with Blender rendering in one process.
 
-**Current direction:** [decision 0004](docs/decisions/0004-single-process-blender-qt.md) supersedes two-process decision 0003. Start with [HOST-001](docs/spikes/0001-qt-eevee-host.md), then follow the [ordered feature/demo queue](replica/feature-order.csv) and [roadmap](docs/roadmap.md). Work locally; no push. HOST-001 now passes on Linux/RTX 3090: Qt 6.8.3 and EEVEE render in one PID, with live roughness/orbit/resize and clean shutdown. [Run the native host](docs/host-linux-run.md), [result](verification/host/host-linux.json).
+Paint in 3D and UV views, organize layers and masks, work with texture sets and UDIMs, import textures and Blender materials, and save editable projects as `.blend` files. Material Presets and Mask Generators provide reusable authoring workflows. Imports of user-owned `.spmsk` files are a compatibility feature; unsupported source operations are reported by the importer.
 
-The current native host also supports OBJ projects, separate Texture Sets, fill/paint layers,
-multichannel 3D/UV strokes, atomic stroke undo, and editable packed `.blend` Save/Open.
-The 2D pane shows unlit texture tiles with UV contours. Start it with
-`distrobox enter bts-build -- bash -lc 'bash /home/mlind/bts/mpainter/scripts/host/run-host.sh --workspace'`.
-The [native run guide](docs/host-linux-run.md) describes the current implementation and file format;
-the prototype notes below describe earlier experiments.
+The application starts with an empty material library. [Download free materials from Poly Haven](https://polyhaven.com/textures): its materials are CC0. Unpack downloads, then import or drop the image files into Assets. Nothing is downloaded automatically.
 
-**Existing prototype evidence, retained while worker development is paused:** constant-fill materials plus bounded Linux native painting and surface-coverage experiments. This is not a finished Painter replica. A genuine Blender EEVEE view is hosted in a separate Linux/X11 Qt experiment. A shared single-image native brush adapter passes gesture, history, cancellation and stock/add-on file round trips; see [painting evidence](verification/painting/README.md). The Painter-like shell, Mac source-fork host and production brush are separate unfinished work. The full product remains the [standing goal](GOAL.md), tracked in [issue 7](https://github.com/mattiaslind93/mpainter/issues/7).
+Build and packaging instructions are in [docs/building.md](docs/building.md). Linux is the locally tested platform. Windows CI is prepared but unverified. The macOS native viewport requires a Metal integration port; no working macOS release is claimed.
 
-The local goal, roadmap and ordered queue are the current implementation instructions. Earlier GitHub issues remain historical until a future authorized update; this architecture change is not published remotely.
+The supplied splash artwork and Mattias Lind’s m-mark icon establish mPainter's own identity. Source and asset attributions are in [NOTICE.md](NOTICE.md); see [LICENSE](LICENSE) for GPL-3.0.
 
-## What is here
-
-- [Painter reconnaissance](replica/recon.md), [153-feature inventory](replica/features.csv) and captured [screens](replica/screens/), distinguishing the installed Painter 6.2.2 from current documentation.
-- [Blender source analysis](docs/research/blender-grounding.md), [ArmorPaint source analysis](docs/research/armorpaint-grounding.md), two independent [architecture candidates](prototypes/) and their [review](prototypes/architecture-review.md).
-- [Measured interface design](replica/design.md), [design tokens](replica/design-tokens.json), [roadmap](docs/roadmap.md) and [decision log](docs/decisions.tsv).
-- A real Qt shell and shared validated layer document, a stock-Blender material adapter, an ordinary Blender add-on, and an isolated main-thread development bridge.
-- A bounded native texture-paint adapter and [surface-brush investigation](docs/research/surface-brush-grounding.md), testing hidden folds, nearby sheets and far rear surfaces independently.
-- Generated [UV/UDIM fixtures](fixtures/README.md) in `.blend`, OBJ, FBX and GLB, plus [verification results](verification/README.md).
-
-## Verified behavior
-
-Fifteen unit tests pass: nine document tests and six native-color startup boundary tests. The actual installed Blender created native layer/material data, saved and reread a `.blend`, and produced a real EEVEE render. Fourteen native-file/material/color checks and eight artist-context checks passed. Add-on registration, add/mask/undo operators and unregistration passed on an isolated fixture. File-based render/save bridge requests also passed.
-
-Painter imported the OBJ and two-tile FBX. Texture export wrote six actual PNGs; the seventh requested output, Mixed AO, was unavailable without mesh-map baking. The evidence records that partial result rather than inferring completion from the success banner.
-
-The subsequent UDIM baking run completed seven mesh-map families and exported all fourteen PNGs, including AO for both tiles. Our own constant-map exporter independently passed eight numerical/file checks and eleven context-preservation checks: five float32 OpenEXRs, ACEScg color, raw data, HDR/negative values and failed-export recovery.
-
-![Actual EEVEE material proof](verification/fill-preview.png)
-
-The image above is a **rendered still**, not an embedded viewport. The Mac prototype now passes offscreen Qt checks in PySide6/Qt 6.12.0; the new native host targets VFX Reference Platform CY2026 / Qt 6.8.x. The user's external [Mac headless run](verification/environment/headless-macos/README.md) also passed real EEVEE/Studio Light on Metal. Neither result proves same-process Qt presentation or painting performance.
-
-The subsequent Linux/X11 experiment passes 17 checks against a real Blender child window inside Qt: native orbit/pan/zoom, visible geometry and material changes, resizing from 976×760 to 1136×860, native save and clean worker exit. The view below is an actual screenshot after editing and resizing. The test uses Mesa software rendering, two processes and a small generated fixture. It does not establish the chosen Mac/source-fork architecture or painting performance. [Runtime evidence and limitations](verification/engine/README.md).
-
-![Real EEVEE embedded in the Linux Qt experiment](verification/engine/passed/host/embedded-after.png)
-
-## Architecture direction
-
-The next paint unit passes 40 native-host checks and eight runtime stages. Native X11 pointer events paint a 512×512 float ACEScg image inside Qt; whole-image undo/redo, Escape, closing during a held stroke, dirty packing, fresh stock reopening, packaged add-on re-edit and a further fresh reopen pass. Experimental Sculpt image painting covers the hidden fold test without painting the far rear witness, but still paints nearby disconnected sheets. It remains an isolated candidate. [Results, real screenshots and limitations](verification/painting/README.md).
-
-![Actual Qt-hosted EEVEE painting](verification/painting/passed/host/paint-two-strokes.png)
-
-The selected destination is a Blender source fork with Qt and a real Blender view region in one process. The [first spike](docs/spikes/0001-qt-eevee-host.md) isolates native surface, event-loop and GPU-context integration. After that, match Painter one feature at a time and deliver a short demo for each. The official Blender source is the primary technical resource; its existing painter is a reference to adapt, not our final layer/brush engine.
-
-ArmorPaint uses its own Iron/Kore engine and immediate-mode UI. Its `.blend` importer runs Blender to convert geometry to OBJ; it is not an EEVEE host or native `.blend` project editor. We study its multichannel GPU painting, packed channels and undo patterns without changing the Blender-core requirement.
-
-## Language direction
-
-Use C for the performance-critical paint/tile/buffer core, GPU shaders for parallel texture work, and C++/Objective-C++ for Qt and Blender hosting. Python remains prototype and add-on orchestration. The current reference calls Blender's existing C++ CPU painter, with Blender owning the pixels and gesture history. See [native-core decision](docs/decisions/0001-native-core.md). The current native host now has its own sparse C++ multichannel paint core; GPU rasterization remains future work.
-
-## ACEScg foundation
-
-Schema 2 authors color in scene-linear ACEScg, preserving finite HDR and negative RGB values. Roughness, metallic, normal, height and masks remain Non-Color numeric data. Other authored working spaces are deferred. The compatibility adapter verifies Blender's active OCIO configuration and converts derived color values into an existing host's actual working space without changing the user's Main.
-
-The isolated Linux runtime initializes a new Main in native ACEScg before authoring. A fresh stock Blender process restores that space from the saved `.blend`, with two packed float images, stock materials and editable fill-layer identities intact after the external images are removed. This is a small two-pixel color/data proof; portable UDIM painting remains unverified. See [color decision](docs/decisions/0002-acescg.md), [runtime experiment](docs/engine-spike-plan.md) and [policy](config/color-policy.json).
-
-## Run
-
-See [docs/run.md](docs/run.md) for Qt startup, the Blender console verification, isolated bridge and add-on packaging. The test bridge is stopped after the recorded run. The user's original Blender scene and existing BlenderTexture add-on remain separate.
-
-Source license: GPL-3.0-or-later. See [NOTICE.md](NOTICE.md) for the separate status of reference screenshots and third-party projects. The installable add-on contains no Painter captures or resources.
